
"smart_sources:2026-07-23 - Stibnite opponents continue to bring legal challenges.md": {"path":"2026-07-23 - Stibnite opponents continue to bring legal challenges.md","last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"last_read":{"hash":"doa1ad","at":1785795033888},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1785188065059,"size":10300,"at":1785795033964,"hash":"doa1ad"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,9],"#":[10,40]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Troy Oppie","target":"Troy Oppie","line":5},{"title":"The view looking south from atop the 'Hecla Heap,' a pile of mining tailings left by the most recent mining period, which ended in the mid-1990s. Perpetua plans to remove and reprocess the tailings to extract remaining gold, and create a new mining area here called the 'Hangar Flats pit' to mine the hillside above (not pictured but to the right). In the distance is where Perpetua plans its tailings storage, though it will create a lined and buttressed area to prevent contamination. Meadow Creek, also in the picture, will be re-routed.","target":"https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/b5b8377/2147483647/strip/true/crop/1620x1080+0+0/resize/1760x1174!/format/webp/quality/90/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb4%2Fcc%2Fd48b178e4c47961cd5da7a562c7d%2Fimg-6095.JPG","line":10,"embedded":true},{"title":"sued in federal court last year","target":"https://www.boisestatepublicradio.org/environment/2025-02-19/stibnite-perpetua-antimony-central-idaho-lawsuit","line":14},{"title":"Idaho","target":"Idaho","line":20}],"metadata":{"title":"Stibnite opponents continue to bring legal challenges","source":"https://www.boisestatepublicradio.org/news/2026-07-23/stibnite-gold-perpetua-legal-challenges?utm_source=newsletters.idahocapitalsun.com&utm_medium=newsletter&utm_campaign=state-audits-kamiah-s-financial-procedures-bonneville-sheriff-urges-local-control-in-ice-agreements&_bhlid=94599e717913b064151b77f1d4304b69963b1403","author":["[[Troy Oppie]]"],"published":"2026-07-23","created":"2026-07-24","description":"Multiple conservation groups sued in federal court last year to overturn the Forest Service approval of the Perpetua Resources mining plan. That lawsuit is still active, but the request that the court stop construction activities while the legal challenge plays out was denied, and they have appealed that denial to the Ninth Circuit.","tags":["#idaho"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},